ne","evidence":"No tie rods and no ring beam at the first-floor level of unit 2: the beams were simply supported on the walls, and their connection was added only in the strengthened configuration (Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. 2024a, Sections 2.3 and 2.4)."}],"MasonryTypes":[{"name":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","description":"Double-leaf masonry of undressed, irregular sandstone (Credaro Berrettino stone) in approximately horizontal courses, with stone chips and mortar filling the core and through stones only at corners and opening edges; the typology of historic aggregates in Basel.","unit_dimensions":"medium","unit_shape":"roughly_cut","unit_material":"irregular_hard_stone","mortar_quality":"lime","horizontal_joints":"partially_continuous","vertical_joints":"partially_staggered","wall_connections":"none","evidence_unit_dimensions":"Stones of 10 to 25 cm in the half-scale specimen (Tomic et al. 2024a, Section 2.1), so 20 to 50 cm at full scale: medium.","evidence_unit_shape":"Undressed, irregular stones, more irregular than those of the earlier Pavia specimen (Tomic et al. 2024a, Section 2.1; Fig. 5a-b): roughly cut.","evidence_unit_material":"Credaro Berrettino stone, a sandstone with a compressive strength of 144 MPa (Tomic et al. 2024b, Table 4): hard stone, not squared.","evidence_mortar_quality":"Commercial hydraulic lime mortar with EPS spheres added to halve stiffness and strength for the scale (Tomic et al. 2024a, Section 2.1). At full scale the mortar it stands for is a weak lime mortar, so it is scored as lime and not as hydraulic lime.","evidence_horizontal_joints":"Stones arranged in approximately horizontal courses (Tomic et al. 2024a, Section 2.1): partially continuous.","evidence_vertical_joints":"Not described in the text; from the masonry texture of Fig. 5a-b the vertical joints are partly staggered.","evidence_wall_connections":"No interlocking between the leaves except through stones at opening edges and building corners (Tomic et al. 2024a, Section 2.1; blind prediction study, poor interlocking): none in the body of the wall.","evidence":"","flags":"Classified at full scale: the specimen is half-scale with EPS-modified mortar, so the properties derived here are to be compared with the measured ones brought back to full scale, not with the measured ones directly.\\nVertical joint staggering is read from the published photographs, not stated in the text.\\nThrough stones exist at corners and opening edges; counting them as sparse headers instead of none raises the quality index (upper variant).","density_kg_m3":"1980","density_note":"Measured masonry density of the same typology, 1980 kg/m3 (Tomic et al. 2024b, Table 4); the density is not scaled by the similitude law adopted.","reference_category":"Muratura a conci sbozzati (roughly cut stone masonry), Circular No. 7/2019, Table C8.5.I","reference_note":"Code class closest to the typology, for comparison only.","variant_lower":"unit_shape=rubble","variant_upper":"wall_connections=sparse"}],"Measured":[{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"compressive_strength_MPa","value":"1.37","basis":"specimen (SERA-AIMS)","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024a), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5963\X2\2013\X0\5991, doi:10.1007/s10518-023-01810-y, CC BY 4.0, Table 1, vertical compression of wallettes"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"tensile_strength_MPa","value":"0.21","basis":"specimen (SERA-AIMS)","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024a), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5963\X2\2013\X0\5991, doi:10.1007/s10518-023-01810-y, CC BY 4.0, Table 1, diagonal compression of wallettes"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"cohesion_MPa","value":"0.29","basis":"specimen (SERA-AIMS)","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024a), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5963\X2\2013\X0\5991, doi:10.1007/s10518-023-01810-y, CC BY 4.0, Table 1"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"compressive_strength_MPa","value":"1.3","basis":"specimen (Pavia, same typology)","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0, Table 4"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"young_modulus_MPa","value":"3462","basis":"specimen (Pavia, same typology)","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0, Table 4"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"shear_modulus_MPa","value":"1524","basis":"specimen (Pavia, same typology), vertical compression","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0, Table 4"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"shear_modulus_MPa","value":"1898","basis":"specimen (Pavia, same typology), diagonal compression","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0, Table 4"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"density_kg_m3","value":"1980","basis":"specimen (Pavia, same typology)","source":"Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0, Table 4"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"compressive_strength_MPa","value":"2.74","basis":"full scale, twice the specimen value (EPS mortar halves stiffness and strength; scale factor to be checked)","source":"2 \X2\00D7\X0\ 1.37 MPa, Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024a), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5963\X2\2013\X0\5991, doi:10.1007/s10518-023-01810-y, CC BY 4.0"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"young_modulus_MPa","value":"6924","basis":"full scale, twice the specimen value (EPS mortar halves stiffness and strength; scale factor to be checked)","source":"2 \X2\00D7\X0\ 3462 MPa, Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"shear_modulus_MPa","value":"3048","basis":"full scale, twice the specimen value (EPS mortar halves stiffness and strength; scale factor to be checked), vertical compression","source":"2 \X2\00D7\X0\ 1524 MPa, Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"shear_modulus_MPa","value":"3796","basis":"full scale, twice the specimen value (EPS mortar halves stiffness and strength; scale factor to be checked), diagonal compression","source":"2 \X2\00D7\X0\ 1898 MPa, Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024b), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5993\X2\2013\X0\6035, doi:10.1007/s10518-022-01582-x, CC BY 4.0"},{"masonry_type":"Double_leaf_stone_masonry","quantity":"shear_strength_turnsek_cacovic_MPa","value":"0.28","basis":"full scale, twice the specimen value (EPS mortar halves stiffness and strength; scale factor to be checked), from f_t / 1.5","source":"2 \X2\00D7\X0\ 0.21 / 1.5 MPa, Tomi\X2\0107\X0\ et al. (2024a), Bull Earthquake Eng 22:5963\X2\2013\X0\5991, doi:10.1007/s10518-023-01810-y, CC BY 4.0"}]}}'),$);
